title: Microsoft Hyper-V Cluster: General information
agents: windows
catalog: os/services
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check shows the name, the IP address and the quorum configuration of a
 Microsoft Windows failover cluster running Hyper-V.

 The check is always {OK}.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_cluster.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V".

discovery:
 One service is created if the agent reports a cluster name.

cluster:
 Every node of the failover cluster reports the cluster, so without a Checkmk
 cluster host the service is created on every node. In a Checkmk cluster host
 the report of the first node, in the order of the node names, is used.
